<title>USA: Elbit aims to supply avionics to Romania.</title>
<headline>Elbit aims to supply avionics to Romania.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's Elbit Ltd said on Thursday that its Romanian subsidiary will negotiate a contract supply avionics systems for helicopters to be purchased by the Romanian Ministry of Defense.</p>
<p>Romania has signed a contract for the acquisition of 96 AH 1 RO &quot;Dracula&quot; helicopters, Elbit said.</p>
<p>The production line for the Dracula helicopters will be established at IAR Brasov SA, Elbit said. Textron Inc had agreed to acquire a 70 percent stake of IAR Brasov, a move that could help Romania's entry into NATO.</p>
<p>The Dracula helicopters are a Romainian version of the twin-engine AH-1W Super Cobra aircraft used by U.S. Marines.</p>
<p>S.C. A-E Electronics SA, in which Elbit owns a majority stake, is also owned by Romania's S.C. Aerostar SA, Elbit said. A-E Electronics is anticipated to enter into operations in the near future, Elbit said.</p>
</text>
